[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_nykq7")
name = "Magic"
text = "Kamen Rider Wizard is the superhero alter ego of Haruto Soma (played by Shunya Shiraishi), the main protagonist of Toei Company's 2012–2013 Japanese tokusatsu series of the same name. • Background: Haruto is a former professional soccer player who survives a solar eclipse ritual called \"The Sabbath\". Surviving grants him magical potential and the ability to channel the mana of his inner Phantom, Wizardragon.• Transformation: Given the Wizardriver belt and Wizard Rings by the mysterious White Wizard (Sou Fueki), Haruto scans rings across the belt's hand unit to transform and cast spells.• Combat & Forms: He combines swordplay, acrobatics, and martial arts with gemstone-themed elemental styles—Flame (ruby/fire), Hurricane (emerald/wind), Water (sapphire/water), and Land (citrine/earth)—alongside Dragon forms and Infinity Style (diamond/light)."
funfacts = Array[String](["Kamen Rider Wizard is the superhero alter ego of Haruto Soma (played by Shunya Shiraishi), the main protagonist of Toei Company's 2012–2013 Japanese tokusatsu series of the same name. • Background: Haruto is a former professional soccer player who survives a solar eclipse ritual called \"The Sabbath\". Surviving grants him magical potential and the ability to channel the mana of his inner Phantom, Wizardragon.• Transformation: Given the Wizardriver belt and Wizard Rings by the mysterious White Wizard (Sou Fueki), Haruto scans rings across the belt's hand unit to transform and cast spells.• Combat & Forms: He combines swordplay, acrobatics, and martial arts with gemstone-themed elemental styles—Flame (ruby/fire), Hurricane (emerald/wind), Water (sapphire/water), and Land (citrine/earth)—alongside Dragon forms and Infinity Style (diamond/light).", "Magic is the use of beliefs, rituals, or sleight of hand to influence events, invoke supernatural forces, or create illusions of the impossible.As a Britannica overview notes, the term spans practices like divination, spells, and stage conjuring, while Wikipedia", "Honda Tadakatsu (March 17, 1548 – December 3, 1610), also known as Honda Heihachirō, was a Japanese samurai, general, and daimyō (feudal lord) who served Tokugawa Ieyasu from the late Sengoku period into the early Edo period. He was one of the Tokugawa Four Heavenly Kings (Tokugawa Shitennō) alongside Ii Naomasa, Sakakibara Yasumasa, and Sakai Tadatsugu.Key Facts & Career• Lifespan & Origins: Born in Mikawa Province in 1548 and died in Edo in 1610 at age 62.• Military Record: Participated in over 50 military campaigns—including Anegawa (1570), Mikatagahara (1572), Nagashino (1575), Komaki and Nagakute (1584), and Sekigahara (1600)—reportedly without ever suffering a serious wound.• Signature Gear: Known for wielding the Tonbokiri (\"Dragonfly Cutter\") spear and the Nakatsukasa sword, riding his horse Mikuniguro, and wearing black lacquer armor with a helmet topped by deer antlers.• Domains & Later Life: Served as daimyō of Ōtaki Domain and later Kuwana Domain before retiring in 1609, passing Kuwana to his son Tadamasa. His daughter Komatsuhime married Sanada Nobuyuki, and his son Tadatomo became daimyō of Ōtaki."])
